   "rule_summary": "The maximum allowed failure rate is 8% for each model. A model exceeding 8% shall not be placed on the market, and any affected marketed model shall undergo regulator-directed corrective action and retesting before continued sale.",
   "comparison": "weakened by: permanent_limit_pct",
   "final_rule_text": "Each model shall undergo a validated sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market entry and at least every three years or after a material design change. The maximum allowed failure rate is 8% for each model. A model exceeding 8% shall not be placed on the market, and any affected marketed model shall undergo regulator-directed corrective action and retesting before continued sale. Manufacturers shall submit per-model test methods and complete results to regulators and disclose results to current and prospective customers of that model, including the test date, failure rate, and any required safety limitations or corrective actions. Results shall not be published in a manner identifying an individual company or model; regulators may publish aggregated, non-identifying results."
  },
