   "comparison": "weakened by: recall_mandatory, permanent_trigger_per_100k, corrective_alternative",
   "final_rule_text": "Before purchase, customers shall receive clear information on thermal risks, installation and maintenance requirements, emergency actions, and available safety updates. Manufacturers shall promptly notify owners and occupants of material newly identified hazards and provide interim precautions; notices of an urgent hazard shall be issued within 72 hours of identification. When any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in any 12-month period, the manufacturer shall promptly notify the regulator and provide incident-rate calculations and supporting data. The regulator shall review the information and may require corrective action or a recall, taking account of incident severity, investigation evidence, and the model’s risk. Regulators may require a recall at any rate where a serious hazard warrants it. Within 72 hours of initiating a recall, the manufacturer shall notify affected customers and the regulator of the recall and its remedy."
